      "writtenOn": "2025-05-15T13:50:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This comment isn\u0027t quite right.  The current code for `textureMaskSpace` is creating the matrix to map from local coords -\u003e mask coords -\u003e texture coords, which is what we want, but nothing needs to be inverted here.\n\nThe gotcha is that this call to `AsFragmentProcessor` (or `MakeFragmentProcessorFromView`) expects a matrix that maps from local coords -\u003e texture coords, whereas FPs created for the SkPaint normally define matrices that map from texture/shading coords -\u003e local coords.  So the matrix we are constructing directly *is* the inverse of what would normally be set on an SkShader.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 487,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 489,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "0d879a07586ee84b4d35e605ba5644150f7c5089",
